{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 22, :comments [{:quotes [{:he "לא תאחר", :translit "lo te'acher", :gloss "you shall not delay"} {:he "לא תאחר לשלמו", :translit "lo te'acher leshalmo", :gloss "you shall not delay to fulfill it"} {:he "מלאתך ודמעך לא תאחר", :translit "me'atecha ve'dim'acha lo te'acher", :gloss "your fullness and your tears you shall not delay"} {:he "כאשר תדור נדר לא תאחר לשלמו", :translit "ka'asher tador neder lo te'acher leshalmo", :gloss "when you vow a vow you shall not delay to fulfill it"} {:he "וישועתי לא תאחר", :translit "vi'shu'ati lo te'acher", :gloss "and my salvation shall not be delayed"} {:he "הנודר ואינו משלם הוא מרחיק ישועה", :translit "ha'noder ve'eino meshalem hu marchikh yeshu'ah", :gloss "one who vows and does not fulfill, he distances salvation"}], :mechanisms [{:kind :other, :note "Gezerah shavah linking three verses sharing the phrase לא תאחר, deriving a cause-effect relationship between fulfilling vows and the timing of salvation"}], :frame {:text "The phrase מלאתך ודמעך לא תאחר appears at Exodus 22:28 in the portion of Mishpatim. Ecclesiastes 5:3 states כאשר תדור נדר לא תאחר לשלמו. Isaiah 46:13 (addressed in chapter 47 context) states וישועתי לא תאחר. The hermeneutical method of gezerah shavah links verses sharing identical phrases; here the repeated לא תאחר establishes a linkage between the commandment to pay vows promptly and the promise of prompt salvation.", :sources ["Exodus 22:28" "Ecclesiastes 5:3" "Isaiah 46:13"]}}], :arithmetic [{:kind :other, :note "Gezerah shavah linking three verses sharing the phrase לא תאחר, deriving a cause-effect relationship between fulfilling vows and the timing of salvation", :by :selah, :ran? false}], :book :deuteronomy, :voice :baal-haturim, :lang :en, :chapter 23, :discipline "bht-chalkboard-v1", :timestamp "2026-07-12T23:38:45.070381727Z", :model "glm-5.2"}